### SECRET IDENT — dual-path honesty
| Probe | check | emit-c | emit-llvm | Dual-path secret? |
|-------|-------|--------|-----------|-------------------|
| `println(tok)` | **SECRET** | **SECRET** | **SECRET** | **yes** |
| `eprintln(tok)` | **SECRET** | **SECRET** | **SECRET** | **yes** |
| `print_err(tok)` | **TYPE** `undefined 'print_err'` | **SECRET** `print_err sink refuses` | **rc=0** `call @print_err` | **no** (emit secret / check type / llvm open) |
| `log(tok)` | **TYPE** `undefined 'log'` | **SECRET** | **rc=0** `call @log` | **no** |
| `fprintf(tok)` | **TYPE** | **SECRET** | **rc=0** `call @fprintf` | **no** |
| `syslog(tok)` | **TYPE** | **SECRET** | **rc=0** `call @syslog` | **no** |
| `print(tok)` | **TYPE** `undefined 'print'` | **rc=0** `print(tok);` no secret | **rc=0** `oo_print_str` + `oo_println` | **no** (llvm println-shape) |
| `println("prefix", tok)` / concat | **SECRET** | **SECRET** | **SECRET** | **yes** |
| `eprintln("prefix", tok)` / concat / escaped lit + ident | **SECRET** | **SECRET** | **SECRET** | **yes** |
| `print_err("prefix", tok)` / concat | **TYPE** | **SECRET** | **rc=0** | **no** |
| `log("prefix", tok)` | **TYPE** | **SECRET** | **rc=0** | **no** |
| `let f = println; f(tok)` | **SECRET** | **SECRET** | **SECRET** | **yes** (front-door alias) |
| `let f = eprintln; f(tok)` | **SECRET** | **SECRET** | **SECRET** | **yes** |
| `let f = print_err; f(tok)` | **TYPE** | **ABORT 134** tcache | **ABORT 134** | fail-closed crash; **not** secret |
| `let f = log; f(tok)` | **TYPE** | **ABORT 134** | **ABORT 134** | same host hole as 6.1 |
| `let z = println(tok)` expr | **SECRET** | **SECRET** | **SECRET** | **yes** (front-door; never reaches guard) |
| `eprintln(pubt)` public + unused SECRET | **OK** | **OK** | **OK** | control |
| `env_set(..., tok)` order control | **CAP** (no `ERR secret`) | **SECRET** | **SECRET** | **no** — ELF type/cap **before** secret |

println/eprintln SECRET **dies at the front-door token walker**
(`process_exit`) before stmt-vs-free-call split. Live eprintln refuse
is **not** proof stmt println was unified onto the guard.

